1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This video is sponsored by Omniverse Connector.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Marvelous Designer 12.1 is now compatible with the USD file format and Omniverse Connector.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Click the copy button in the upper right corner of any window to open the Omniverse Connector window and the USD layer window.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Drag these windows to the right position.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Click the Create button in the window of the USD layer window to save the path and name to create an empty USD file.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The newly created file will automatically be set to authoring layer.usd.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Please note that you can create multiple USD layers,

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,000
but you can only change one of them.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:08,000
If you want to edit the selected USD file under the authoring layer,

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:22,000
please select the 3D or 2D window of the USD file and then click the button in the upper right corner of any window to export it to the USD layer.

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
If there is no authoring layer at the moment,

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
please click the Create button in the window of the USD layer window to create a new one.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
After setting up the PREM path, you can export the clothes.

14
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
According to the 3D clothing rendering style when exporting, the results will be different.

15
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
If the current 3D clothing rendering style is a thick texture surface,

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
then it will export the clothes with thickness.

17
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
If you want to export all the objects in the scene at the same time,

18
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,000
please go to the file in the main menu and export to USD.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,000
When exporting the USD window, please select the object type you want to export.

20
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,000
At this time, you can choose to export thin or thick, and set the PREM path to complete the export.

21
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You can import the import button in the window of the USD layer window to import the USD file,

22
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
or you can import the file in the main menu to import the USD file.

23
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
In the window of the USD layer window,

24
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
select the download type and object type.

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
If you want to import it as a virtual model,

26
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
you can choose to automatically create a test穿服.

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Now the USD file has been successfully imported.

28
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
The grid and the material have appeared in the USD layer window,

29
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
and it is automatically exported to the main menu.

30
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
In the next step, you can import the 3D clothing rendering style.

31
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
In the next step, you can import the 3D clothing rendering style.

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
In the next step, you can import the 3D clothing rendering style.

33
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
The 3D clothing rendering style has been set to be an Authoring layer.

34
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:00,000
The 3D clothing rendering style is now set to Authoring layer.

35
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,000
If you would like to save the objects in the current scene

36
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
and add an extra block to the USD file,

37
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:13,000
please replace the plus option in the UD window.

38
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Or, like in the video,

39
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
and enter the file in the menu to add a new layer of U.S.D.

40
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Click the Clear button to clear all layers in the U.S.D. layer window

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
However, you can still find these objects in the 3D window

42
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
because they are the object of the scene

43
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:52,000
First, you need to connect to the Omniverse server

44
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Please click the icon in the upper right corner of the Omniverse Connector window

45
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
and select Add Server in the drop-down menu

46
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Enter the name of the server you want to connect to and click Add Server

47
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
As a reference, I entered localhost here

48
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Please note that in order to use Omniverse Connector, Omniverse Create

49
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:14,000
you need to connect to the same server of Marvelous Designer

50
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Open a U.S.D. file in Omniverse Create

51
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Please note that in order to import text and objects at the same time

52
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
please make sure that the text folder and the U.S.D. folder are stored in the same path

53
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:35,000
In the Live menu in the upper right corner of the window, select Create Drawing

54
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:40,000
In the Live Session, click the name of the drawing in the window

55
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
A new drawing will be created

56
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:53,000
In Marvelous Designer, open the same U.S.D. file you opened in Omniverse Create

57
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Now in Marvelous Designer, you can enter the drawing you created in Omniverse Create

58
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Click the Omniverse Connector icon to enter the drawing

59
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Select the name of the drawing created in Omniverse Create and click Add

60
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
After successfully entering the drawing

61
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Go back to the U.S.D. layer window

62
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
A Live Session layer will appear

63
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
If another participant is adding your drawing

64
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
You can also click the refresh participant button to refresh participant information

65
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:40,000
When the Live Session layer set to Authoring is exported to the U.S.D. operation

66
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,000
You will see the file update in Omniverse Create

67
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
When the Live Session layer is set to Authoring

68
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
You can also click the refresh participant button to refresh participant information

69
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:57,000
However, when the normal U.S.D. layer set to Authoring is exported to the U.S.D. layer

70
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:01,000
These changes will not affect the objects in Omniverse Create

71
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:06,000
When the BaseUSD file is in the window

72
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Click the Fetch button to synchronize the changes in Omniverse Create

73
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
If you need to leave the current drawing

74
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Please open Omniverse Connect

75
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
And click on the Leave Drawing menu below

76
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:42,839
After clicking the Leave Drawing button, click the View

